## Code Generation Guidelines

- Use `from __future__ import annotations` at the top of every module.
- Use `pathlib.Path` for all filesystem paths — never `os.path`.
{% if logging_enabled %}
- Use `get_logger(name)` from `{{ pkg_name }}.logging` for diagnostics — never raw `print()`.
{% endif %}
{% if logging_enabled or env_parsing == "dotenv" %}
- Read environment variables with `get_env(key)` from `{{ pkg_name }}.env` — never `os.environ.get()`.
{% endif %}
- Catch specific exceptions — never bare `except:` or silent `except ...: pass`.
- Use f-strings for all string interpolation.
- Type-annotate all public functions.

---

## Anti-Patterns to Avoid

{% if logging_enabled or env_parsing == "dotenv" %}
- ❌ Do not call `os.environ.get()` — use `get_env()` from `{{ pkg_name }}.env`.
{% endif %}
- ❌ Do not use `os.path` — use `pathlib.Path`.
{% if cli_support == "typer" %}
- ❌ Do not apply `@app.command()` in `commands/*.py` — register commands from `__main__.py`.
{% endif %}
{% if db_driver != "none" and db_driver != "nosql" %}
- ❌ Do not write raw SQL outside of `database/migrations/` or `database/seeders/`.
{% endif %}
